  "definition": "A silicon-based multichannel probe is an implantable device comprising multiple electrodes (also referred to as recording sites) made from a silicon semiconductor material, designed for use in neural tissue, which enables the simultaneous recording of the electrical activity of multiple neurons within the same or different layers of the brain.",
